      "lineNbr": 486,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-13T21:54:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The file content is stored in a map for all devices, but it is stopped as soon as we find the device we are looking for.\n\nIn the end we never know how much of the file has been parsed or not, and we need to check for the file every time.\n\nI think we should either load the file once and never read it again from it during the session, or read it each time and do not use 2 static Map for it\n\nI am also not a big fan of having the file parsing in both native and Java. Can\u0027t we implement it only once and call it from the other side ?",
